    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is Canva better than Adobe Express?</h3>
    <p>For most users, Canva is the better choice. It has more templates, a larger free tier, better collaboration, and a more polished mobile app. Adobe Express is better if you already use Adobe Creative Cloud, need Photoshop-quality AI tools, or want tighter integration with Adobe Fonts and Stock. For casual design and social media, Canva wins. For Adobe ecosystem users, Express wins.</p>

    <h3>Is Adobe Express really free?</h3>
    <p>Adobe Express has a free tier that includes limited templates, basic editing tools, and 2 GB of cloud storage. The free tier also includes limited generative AI credits powered by Adobe Firefly. The Premium plan at $9.99 per month unlocks all templates, premium fonts, full Adobe Stock access, and more AI credits. Canva's free tier is more generous with over 250,000 free templates and 5 GB of storage.</p>

    <h3>Can I use Canva and Adobe Express together?</h3>
    <p>Yes, and many creators do. A common workflow is to use Adobe Express for AI image generation and Photoshop-style edits, then import the assets into Canva for template-based design and team collaboration. Both tools export standard formats like PNG, JPG, and PDF. Canva's collaboration features are stronger, so most teams use Canva as the primary tool and Adobe Express for specialized AI tasks.</p>

    <h3>Which is better for social media design?</h3>
    <p>Canva is better for social media design. It has more platform-specific templates (Instagram posts, stories, TikTok covers, YouTube thumbnails), a content planner for scheduling posts, and Magic Write for generating captions. Adobe Express has similar templates but fewer options and no built-in content scheduling. For social media managers, Canva is the clear winner.</p>

    <h3>Does Adobe Express include Photoshop?</h3>
    <p>No, Adobe Express does not include Photoshop. It is a separate, lighter design tool focused on templates and quick edits. However, Adobe Express Premium is included with Creative Cloud All Apps subscriptions, so Photoshop users get Express at no extra cost. Express also includes some Photoshop-powered AI tools like Generative Fill and background removal, but it is not a full Photoshop replacement.</p>

    <h3>Which has better AI features?</h3>
    <p>Adobe Express has stronger AI image generation through Adobe Firefly, which produces higher-quality images and is commercially safe because it was trained on licensed content. Canva has more AI features overall including Magic Write, Magic Edit, Magic Eraser, and Magic Design, but the image generation quality is slightly below Firefly. For AI image quality, Adobe Express wins. For AI workflow breadth, Canva wins.</p>

